{{ steps "Checkout" "checkout" }}

{{with .Problem}}
--panel[padding=12, margin=0 0 8 0, border=1, color=accent, radius=8]--
{{.}}
--/panel--
{{end}}

{{- /*
One choice, two cards, and nothing else on the page until it is made.

The description of each way to pay lives behind the question mark on its
card. It is the reason to pick one and it is also four lines of prose in the
middle of a decision that is really made on one word and one icon: somebody
who knows what Lightning is should not have to read past it, and somebody who
does not has a mark to press. See markdown_paypick.dart.
*/}}
{{if .Methods.Both}}
--paypick[title=How would you like to pay?, action=/setCheckout, chosen={{.Checkout.Method}}]--
--option[method=ln, icon=lightning, label=Lightning, note=Settles straight away]--
Settles straight away. Paid from your Bison Relay wallet with one press, and
the seller sees it immediately.
--option[method=onchain, icon=onchain, label=On-chain, note=About five minutes]--
Settles after one confirmation from the network — about five minutes. Pay
from any Decred wallet by scanning a code, or from this one.
--/paypick--
{{else if .Methods.LN}}
--paypick[title=How you will pay, chosen=ln]--
--option[method=ln, icon=lightning, label=Lightning, note=Settles straight away]--
This shop takes Lightning. It settles straight away and is paid from your
Bison Relay wallet with one press.
--/paypick--
{{else if .Methods.OnChain}}
--paypick[title=How you will pay, chosen=onchain]--
--option[method=onchain, icon=onchain, label=On-chain, note=About five minutes]--
This shop takes on-chain payments. They settle after one confirmation from
the network — about five minutes — and can be paid from any Decred wallet.
--/paypick--
{{else}}
--panel[padding=14, border=1, color=outline, radius=8]--
The seller will be in touch with how to pay once the order is placed.
--/panel--
{{end}}

{{if .Ready}}
{{if .Ships}}
## Where should it go?
{{end}}

--form--
type="action" value="/setCheckout"
type="hidden" name="doing" value="continue"
type="hidden" name="method" value="{{.Checkout.Method}}"
{{- if .Ships}}
{{- with .Checkout.Ship}}
type="txtinput" label="Name" name="name" value="{{.Name}}"
type="txtinput" label="Address" name="address1" value="{{.Address1}}"
type="txtinput" label="Address (optional)" name="address2" value="{{.Address2}}"
type="txtinput" label="City" name="city" value="{{.City}}"
type="txtinput" label="State" name="state" value="{{.State}}"
type="txtinput" label="Postal code" name="postalCode" value="{{.PostalCode}}"
type="txtinput" label="Phone (optional)" name="phone" value="{{.Phone}}" help="A phone number is only for whoever delivers this. The seller reaches you in Bison Relay - in this order's own messages."
{{- else}}
type="txtinput" label="Name" name="name"
type="txtinput" label="Address" name="address1"
type="txtinput" label="Address (optional)" name="address2"
type="txtinput" label="City" name="city"
type="txtinput" label="State" name="state"
type="txtinput" label="Postal code" name="postalCode"
type="txtinput" label="Phone (optional)" name="phone" help="A phone number is only for whoever delivers this. The seller reaches you in Bison Relay - in this order's own messages."
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
type="submit" label="Continue to review" style="primary"
--/form--
{{end}}

---

**Total: {{ money .Total }}**{{ with .TotalDCR }} · ≈ {{.}}{{ end }}

{{- /*
What the reader's own wallet can do, put beside what the order comes to.

The shop cannot know this and never learns it: the block reads the balance in
the client that is drawing the page. It is here rather than in the payment
cards because it is one fact about one order, and a buyer deciding between
two ways to pay wants it in the same glance as the total.
*/}}
{{ with .TotalDCRAmount }}--wallet[need={{.}}, show={{ $.WalletShow }}]--
{{ end }}
